cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these workflows, please cite them as below."
type: software
title: "2d-mlip-workflows: DFT dataset generation, fine-tuning of universal machine-learning interatomic potentials and molecular dynamics of 2D carbon materials"
abstract: >-
  Workflows and scripts to build DFT and ab initio molecular dynamics training data
  with Quantum ESPRESSO, select configurations with SOAP descriptors and farthest-point
  sampling, fine-tune universal machine-learning interatomic potentials (MACE, NequIP, PET),
  estimate their uncertainty with committees, and run and analyse NVT and NPT molecular
  dynamics of 2D carbon materials, applied to boron-graphdiyne.
authors:
  - family-names: "Martín Encinar"
    given-names: "Luis"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4839-7604"
    affiliation: "Universidad de Valladolid"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-25"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/luimaren/2d-mlip-workflows"
keywords:
  - machine-learning interatomic potentials
  - fine-tuning
  - MACE
  - density functional theory
  - ab initio molecular dynamics
  - Quantum ESPRESSO
  - 2D materials
  - graphdiyne
